1: # P3K.54. The three actual first-flop classes of the selected-cusp source loop
2: 
3: Proved after full root and independent blind_control audits.
4: 
5: Retain exactly the positive marked rho loop, fixed scalar, finite cap,
6: source periods and line maps of P3F.54/P3F.56. In the initial cusp fan
7: label the curves by the three pairs of actual triangles in OE.1:
8: \(C_0\) is the fixed vertical edge, \(C_1\) the horizontal edge,
9: and \(C_2\) the diagonal edge. The actual oriented return classes
10: after their respective first periodic flops are
11: \[
12:                     (23,23,1)\quad\text{in }\mathbb Z/28.
13: \]
14: We prove this only for these three first flops. It asserts no
15: subsequent common-product reset or general fan formula.
16: 
17: ## FF.1. The three native family stars and their actual maps
18: 
19: For the fixed star \(C_0\) use P3K.40/P3K.42's literal source
20: coordinate and physical normal chart:
21: \[
22:  z=Z=\frac{s-\rho}{s+\rho},\qquad
23:  q=zc_0c_1,\qquad z'=z^{-1},\quad c_i'=zc_i.
24:                                                                \tag{FF.1}
25: \]
26: Its complete normal framing, physical delta action and retained
27: \(q_T/q\) winding are those proved in P3K.40 and P3K.42.
28: 
29: The two other native family stars are also actual coordinate maps,
30: not only normal-bundle identifications. In the six charts OE.4,
31: for \(C_1\) take
32: \[
33:  (z,c_0,c_1)=(c,a,b),\qquad
34:  (z',c'_0,c'_1)=(\eta v,g w,(g\eta)^{-1}u),           \tag{FF.2}
35: \]
36: where \(g\) is the actual source translation multiplier and
37: \(\eta=\lambda\beta\) the actual line/suspension multiplier.
38: Direct substitution of OE.4 gives
39: \(z'=z^{-1}\), \(c'_i=zc_i\). For \(C_2\) use
40: \[
41:  (z,c_0,c_1)=(a,b,c),\qquad (z',c'_0,c'_1)=(u,v,w),  \tag{FF.3}
42: \]
43: with the identical standard transition. The functions in (FF.2)
44: are the original nonzero holomorphic units on the annular source
45: representative, including their initial constants and their given
46: extending logarithms. The transformations are invertible on those
47: charts. They are applied as coordinate arrows to the actual family,
48: so all source-period, finite-cap, line and annular maps are conjugated
49: by those same arrows. None of those data is replaced by a marking
50: chosen only on homology.
51: 
52: In particular, every chosen conifold cell has trivial stabilizer
53: under the period lattice. Choose its quotient representative,
54: make (FF.1), (FF.2) or (FF.3) there, and extend to all translates by
55: the original period maps. This is the same equivariant construction
56: of the periodic flop as P3K.40. The finite cap is outside this cusp
57: neighbourhood and its actual annular identification is retained.
58: The full nonconstant units are transported by their literal common
59: normal-rescaling isotopies on the two small-resolution charts and
60: on their shared punctured conifold. Their endpoint maps are the
61: ones in (FF.1)--(FF.3); no new endpoint translation is inserted.
62: 
63: Each of these native stars therefore has the actual Cox link
64: \[
65:  (S^3_a\times S^3_c)/S^1,\qquad
66:  (a,c)\sim(e^{i\phi}a,e^{-i\phi}c),
67: \]
68: with \(u=a_0+ja_1\), \(v=c_0+j\overline{c_1}\), and
69: \[
70:  h=uiu^{-1},\qquad k=v^{-1}iv,\qquad q_H=uv.
71: \]
72: The old and new products are respectively \((h,q_H)\) and
73: \((k,q_H)\). Their exact common boundary arrow and exterior
74: extension are
75: \[
76:  \tau(h,q_H)=(q_H^{-1}hq_H,q_H),\qquad
77:  T(y,q_H)=(q_H^{-1}yq_H,q_H).                         \tag{FF.4}
78: \]
79: The inverse uses \(q_Hyq_H^{-1}\), so the extension is smooth at
80: \(y=0\) and orientation preserving. This is the actual family arrow
81: as well: all four integer Cox weights obey the unrestricted
82: identity SF.8, which intertwines (FF.4) even when their sum is
83: nonzero. The complete unit isotopies just described carry that
84: identity with their actual boundaries. Thus \(T\) compares the
85: actual positive returns, with no discarded parameter winding.
86: 
87: ## FF.2. The native relative pairs and the resulting central classes
88: 
89: Use exactly K23's relative generators
90: \[
91:  L(y,q_H)=(y,\zeta(y)q_H),\qquad
92:  R(y,q_H)=(y,q_H\zeta(y)),
93: \]
94: with its degree-one \(\zeta\) and its oriented central generator
95: \(\mathcal C\). Their six-sphere classes are zero, while
96: \(\mathcal C\) is the positive generator in this run's convention.
97: The native triples of the original positive source return are
98: \[
99:  \begin{array}{c|rrr}
100:  &m&n&s\\ \hline
101:  C_0&0&-6&1\\
102:  C_1&0&-6&1\\
103:  C_2&-6&0&1.
104:  \end{array}                                             \tag{FF.5}
105: \]
106: The first is P3K.42; the other two are the actual native-star
107: comparison and derivative computation of P3K.50/P3K.52. In
108: particular, the pure-left ordinary-product changes have already
109: been removed by the exact arrows OR.11. The central coordinate is
110: the oriented closed source-loop return one in each case.
111: 
112: K23's exact relative conjugation for the same map (FF.4) is
113: \[
114:  T(L^mR^n\mathcal C^s)T^{-1}
115:        =L^{-n}R^{m+2n}\mathcal C^{s+n}.              \tag{FF.6}
116: \]
117: There is no circle-quotient hypothesis in this identity. We use
118: only the literal local products, the actual exterior extension and
119: the already established native integers. Substitution into (FF.6)
120: gives central coordinates \((-5,-5,1)\), hence precisely
121: \((23,23,1)\) modulo28. If one records the first-resolution complex
122: normal convention after the flop, K31's explicit fixed reflection
123: \(J(q)=k\overline qk^{-1}\), acting by
124: \((y,q_H)\mapsto(Jy,Jq_H)\), swaps the two free integers and
125: preserves the central coordinate. The three resulting native pairs
126: in that convention are \((-12,6),(-12,6),(-6,0)\).
127: 
128: The diagonal value one agrees with the independently constructed
129: half-transport/conjugacy of P3K.45; the proof above did not infer its
130: integer from that agreement. It computes all three first flops
131: from their actual family products. The extension of an arbitrary
132: ordinary plumbing product through a later flop is a separate map
133: and is not asserted here.
